# CAMEL OVERKILL: HUMP-3b "HERALD". Radio announcements for the alert core (split out: a circuit box holds 64 parts).
name camel_herald
box battery
note "HERALD: HOW IT WORKS" "Builds '[CamelOS] ALERT RED | flood: Medbay | fire: none' from the alert name (7205) and the sensor network's room names (7400 flood / 7401 fire, held 10 s).\nIt is sent ONLY when the alert level changes: an Equals of the level against a 0.1 s delayed copy opens a relay for a few ticks. Every channel-0 wifi hears every other one, so a per-tick announcement would drown the crew's radio commands. The chat wifi also waits 20 s between messages.\n'announce off' in CamelOS (7410) silences it."
note "WIRING" "out1 -> chat wifi (channel 0, LinkToChat) signal_in"
c rxn wifi Channel=7205
c rxf wifi Channel=7400
c rxx wifi Channel=7401
c rxa wifi Channel=7410
c flood or TimeFrame=10
c fire or TimeFrame=10
w rxf.out flood.1
w rxx.out fire.1
c froom mem Value=none
c xroom mem Value=none
c fclr check TargetSignal=0 Output=none FalseOutput=""
c xclr check TargetSignal=0 Output=none FalseOutput=""
w rxf.out froom.in
w rxx.out xroom.in
w flood.out fclr.in
w fire.out xclr.in
w fclr.out froom.in
w xclr.out xroom.in
c a0 mem Value="[CamelOS] ALERT "
c a1 concat
c a2 concat Separator=" | flood: "
c a3 concat Separator=" | fire: "
w a0.out a1.1
w rxn.out a1.2
w a1.out a2.1
w froom.out a2.2
w a2.out a3.1
w xroom.out a3.2
c adl delay Delay=0.1
c aeq equals Output=1 FalseOutput=0
c chg not
c men mem Value=1
c open and
c agate relay IsOn=false
w rxa.out men.in
w rxn.out adl.in aeq.1
w adl.out aeq.2
w aeq.out chg.in
w chg.out open.1
w men.out open.2
w open.out agate.set_state
w a3.out agate.1
w agate.signal_out1 out1
